{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1558565-artifacts-of-the-seven-seas","id":1558565,"title":"Artifacts of the Seven Seas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-02-28T18:00:51-08:00","id":1558565,"title":"Artifacts of the Seven Seas","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#101010\">In taverns across the seven seas, stories are told of powerful Artifacts from the Golden Age of Piracy. According to the legends, they are drawn to the adventurous and free-spirited, setting sail with them towards new horizons and legends worth retelling. Some even believe they were made by the same entity that created the Codex, forming a set with it, embodying the connection pirates have with the sea. Even now they await the call of a new brave soul.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Captain's Hoard (\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Gnosis:</span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 4</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Arcana:</span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\"> Matter 5</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Mana Capacity:</span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 14</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Effects: </span></b><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">Endless Bounty</span></i><span style=\"color:#101010\"> , </span><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">Remote Control</span></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Utility Attainments: </b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>Permanence </i></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Description:</span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\"> A key carved from a single piece of petrified coral, it feels heavy in the hand and sturdy, despite being porous. Under the moonlight, an intricate carving of a ship can be seen along its shank, heading away from the bow. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">In order to activate it, the key must be pointed at a subject, or make contacts with it, while the user extends a finger along the shank, &quot;pointing&quot; the direction the ship sails. Turning it clockwise activates </span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>Endless Bounty</i></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> and counterclockwise uses </span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>Remote Control</i></span><span style=\"color:#101010\">. It is said many pirates have used it to arm and supply their troops with plentiful wealth, food, drink and armaments. A few use it to break their crew out of jail, unlock chests of loot or open their path. Some skilled users have even used it to bring their ships to life, making them far deadlier in ship combat, or a living terror against mutineers. Whatever treasure chest, or gate, this Artifact is supposed to unlock, is a Mystery that still challenges many an adventurous soul.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Fair Winds (\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Gnosis:</span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 3</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Arcana: </span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Time 4</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Mana Capacity:</span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 10</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Effects: </span></b><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">Green Light / Red Light</span></i><span style=\"color:#101010\">, </span><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">Veil of Moments</span></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Description:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> A brown tricorne hat made of the full grain leather of a giant, seafaring, bird cryptid. It seems to naturally fall into its shape, without the use of pins, laces or buttons. The interior lining looks like fine wool, but feels like down feathers. It is waxed by the oil the creature used on its feathers, making it completely waterproof. It is always a perfect fit on the user's head and will not fall off by itself, not in strong winds, not when the user dives underwater, or even if they are upside down. However, it does seem to have a sense of humor, as it will fall off if they trip.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">Whenever the user sings or hums a sea shanty, its abilities can be activated. It can allow sea journeys to be made much faster, for treasure hunters to stay ahead of their rivals, or used to sow chaos on one's pursuers. In dire situations, it can allow the crew to survive without rations, persist when there is no time to rest or keep a crewmate alive until a healer can be found.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Fathomless Tide (\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Gnosis:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 2</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Arcana:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> Life 4</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Mana Capacity:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 8</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Effects: </b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>Transform Life</i></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Description:</span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\"> A long coat of excellent quality, which adjusts itself to match the measurements of the user. It is woven out of a midnight blue silk, its interior lined with a golden yellow velvet that is completely waterproof. It has an ornate silver braid trim, with silver buttons engraved with High Speech runes. A stylized depiction of tentacles is embroidered in silvery, serpentine patterns on the sleeves. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">Whenever it is buttoned in a specific sequence, its effect can be activated while it remains closed. It has been used to explore the most remote depths of the ocean, survive in the most inhospitable edges of the map, adapt when fighting a dangerous foe, escape deadly situations and to use devious tactics at sea.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Horizon\u2019s Call (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Gnosis:</span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 2</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Arcana:</span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\"> Fate 3</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Mana Capacity:</span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 6</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Effects: </span></b><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">Serendipity</span></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Description:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> A meticulously crafted nautical compass, with a square case made of oak, with a dark varnish. High Speech runes are carved on all sides. The top of the case has them arranged on a geomantic compass.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">When a user opens the compass with a goal in mind and says in High Speech &quot;show me a new horizon&quot;, the runes glow like blazing coals. If they roll it on a surface (a paper, a table, their arm), it imprints a map guiding the user to their desired goal, with the legends of the map giving tips. Once they use up all the rolls it grants, the map vanishes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Kraken's Eye (\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Gnosis:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 3</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Arcana: </b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\">Space 4</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Mana Capacity:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 12</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Effects: </b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>Scrying</i></span><span style=\"color:#101010\">, </span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>Zoom In</i></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> (as an Unveiling of Space)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Utility Attainments:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> Sympathetic Range</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Description:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> An iron spyglass made of an organic looking material, which is warm to the touch and never corrodes. The length bears intaglios of tentacles reaching out from the objective lens, and both lenses are crystal clear.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">Whenever the user says &quot;Open the eye of the storm&quot;, it causes the lens to become a mossy green cephalopod eye, glowing with an eerie inner light. Looking through the Kraken's Eye in this form allows it to utilize its ability. Navigators have used it to chart a trail through storms, lookouts have used it to spot islands on the horizon or enemy ships, captains use it to scout a location or keep an eye on their enemies.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Parlay's End (\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Gnosis:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 4</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Arcana:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> Space 5, Fate 2</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Mana Capacity:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 16</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Effects: </b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>Banishment </i></span><span style=\"color:#101010\">(Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Fate \u2022\u2022) (see below)</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Utility Attainments:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> Everywhere </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Description:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> A flintlock pistol assembled entirely from interlocking bricks of magnetite loadstone, with a carving of a lung dragon flying down the side plate. It is held together by intense ferromagnetic forces, yet it operates smoothly. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">Although it can be used as a normal flintlock, activating its effect requires the user to place a thumb in the point of the side plate where the dragon coils, before pulling the trigger. When a subject is hit by the spell, they are instantly teleported to where they will be the most delayed. They can end up on a deserted island, a busy tavern, amidst an emotionally charged situation, or in sight of their enemies, in whichever scenario inconveniences them the most. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Red Sky (\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Gnosis:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 3</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Arcana:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> Forces 5</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Mana Capacity:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 12</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Effects: </b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>Control Heat</i></span><span style=\"color:#101010\">, </span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>Environmental Shield</i></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Description:</span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\"> A cutlass made of finely wrought steel, its surface is always polished to a mirror sheen, the occasional ripple appearing in reflections. Its circular handguard has a golden finish, with a stylized engraving of the sun. The handle is made of a deep blue shagreen.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">A user must address it by name, calling upon it as if it were sentient to use its abilities. Wielders invoke its aid when dueling foes, using bitter cold to disorient and weaken opponents without damaging potential loot. Some command it to overheat blades and force foes to disarm. When boarding an enemy vessel, captains will address it as a trusted crewmate, charging it with calling down scorching heat and biting cold upon the deck, weakening their foes even as their own crew fight protected from the effects.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>The Wave's Price (\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Gnosis:</span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 4</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Arcana:</span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\"> Death 4, Matter 4</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Mana Capacity:</span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\"> 16</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Effects: </span></b><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">Castaway's Plunder</span></i><span style=\"color:#101010\"> (see below)</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#101010\">Description:</span></b><span style=\"color:#101010\"> A boarding axe with a head carved out of an ocean blue, crystalline material, which looks like frozen ice. The handle is made out of dense whale bone and wrapped in whale leather. Whenever sunlight hits the axe head, a caustic light pattern dances inside it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">When the user holds it from the bottom of the handle, allowing for the maximum momentum to be built, they can unleash its effect. Any pieces of an object destroyed fall away as salt, and the user can choose to replenish either their stores of mana or the Wave's Price. </span><br /> \u200b</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#101010\">New Spell: Castaway's Plunder (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Practice:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> Unraveling</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Primary Factor:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> Potency </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Withstand: </b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> Durability </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> Larceny, Survival, Weaponry</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\"><b>Description:</b></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> A spell developed by mages during the Golden Age of Piracy, so they could heal and restore their power whenever they found themselves stranded exploring the Mysteries. Whenever an object is hit by this spell, it loses [Potency] Structure as its Pattern is thorn apart and mana is harvested from it. The caster receives an equal amount of mana as the object lost Structure.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>What were you thinking design wise ?</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#101010\">After having worked on a pirate themed Legacy (</span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>The Crystal Navigators</i></span><span style=\"color:#101010\">) and reading </span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>Dark Eras 2: The Devil and the Deep Blue Sea</i></span><span style=\"color:#101010\">, I was inspired to make pirate themed Artifacts. They were designed to represent the equipment of a pirate king, both as a display of their wealth and as the tools they would use in their adventures. The material they were made of and their names would also symbolize their connection to the sea.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">The Captain\u2019s Hoard is a treasure key, inspired by the one Davy Jones had in </span><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">Pirates of the Caribbean: Dead Man\u2019s Chest</span></i><span style=\"color:#101010\">. It allows them to make any treasure chest a source of infinite wealth, it also acts as a skeleton key that can open any lock. It can allow them to take control of their ships, like Blackbeard did in </span><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">Pirates of the Caribbean: On Stranger Tides</span></i><span style=\"color:#101010\">. Lastly, it acts as a potential plot hook, with what it could possibly unlock being deliberately left open.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">Fair Winds is made out of a roc, and is a captain\u2019s hat that is easy to wear in any situation. It can be used to tilt the winds in their favor when time is of the essence, help them get away in high action chases, or allow them to persevere when things get rough. It's named after the idiom </span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>\u201cFair winds and following seas\u201d</i></span><span style=\"color:#101010\">, a blessing sailors use for a smooth and safe voyage.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">Fathomless Tide is a long coat that allows the pirate to be suited to explore any part of the sea. It can allow them to take on a Cthulu-like appearance as well. The design is inspired by Vergil\u2019s trench coat from the </span><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">Devil May Cry</span></i><span style=\"color:#101010\"> games.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">Horizon\u2019s Call is inspired by Jack Sparrow\u2019s compass, as well as the Mao Kun map. It creates a treasure map to anything the pirate seeks. Since it is cast with Fate 3, I imagine it would normally be used with Reach assigned to instant use and using a chosen skill, allowing the pirate to find a path to their goal that best leverages their abilities. The compass case is made out of oak for two reasons. The first is that oak is an antiseptic wood, so getting a splinter won't kill a user, which is why many ships at the time were made of it.The second is because it symbolizes strength, endurance and wisdom. The varnish is used to make it waterproof.</span><br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">Kraken\u2019s Eye is a spyglass that allows them to keep a better lookout on their surroundings than ever before, and is also a powerful tool for scouting. The pirate can also scry on their enemies, helping them stay one step ahead of them. The design is inspired by the Necronomicon cutscene in Cyanide\u2019s </span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>Call of Cthulhu</i></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> game, and it is implied that the Artifact is alive.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">Parlay\u2019s End allows them to teleport away any foes the pirate cannot negotiate with and is not ready to face. The target is even placed in a scenario that keeps them too busy to teleport back or continue to give chase to the pirate. It is made with magnetic loadstones, which could be found at sea, and were used to create compasses. In this way, Parlay\u2019s End is a magnet for trouble to those it shoots. The design is inspired by the Mosaic Culverin from</span><i><span style=\"color:#101010\"> Salt and Sanctuary</span></i><span style=\"color:#101010\">.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">Red Sky is a cutlass that helps a pirate fight dirty. </span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>Control Heat</i></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> can be used to penalize an opponent\u2019s actions by creating an Extreme Environment. When used at higher Potency, it can be used as a constant source of damage, as well as instantly superheat or freeze objects, which has lots of creative applications. </span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>Environmental Shield</i></span><span style=\"color:#101010\"> guarantees that no matter how rough weather gets at sea, the pirate and their crewmates can ride out the storm. The name is based on the old sailor\u2019s adage of </span><span style=\"color:#101010\"><i>\u201cRed Sky at night, sailor\u2019s delight. Red Sky in morning, sailor\u2019s warning\u201d</i></span><span style=\"color:#101010\">. The golden sun engraving symbolizes the ability to create a scorching heat, and the blue shagreen (shark\u2019s leather) represents its ability to call forth a freezing cold. Lastly, the activation command was inspired by Sir Mirror from the Castlevania show, and was suggested by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a>.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">The Wave\u2019s Price is a pirate mage\u2019s survival tool, allowing them to scavenge mana from just about anything. The design is inspired by stalhrim weapons from the </span><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">Elder Scrolls</span></i><span style=\"color:#101010\"> series, and the use of whale bone by the </span><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">Dishonored </span></i><span style=\"color:#101010\">series. </span><br /> <br /> That concludes the design notes, hope you had as much fun reading them as I had writing them. A huge thanks to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> and NuriaAge for all their feedback.<br /> \u200b</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-28-2026, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T06:01:39-08:00","id":1558619,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about <i>Castaway's Plunder</i>. Like, <i>Siphon Integrity</i> was in 1e, and very conspicuously isn't in 2e. Also, the original spell has the proviso that objects below size 3 just don't have enough mana present to have an effect. Seems like this would essentially avoid mana being an issue.<br /> <br /> The artefacts are all pretty fun though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}